    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The crescent shawl curves because you add stitches faster at the outer edge than at the inner edge. Each "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "shell-stitch-l2"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "shell stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " row uses "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "turning-chain-l2"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "turning chains"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at both ends to shape the arc. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "crescent-shaping-l2"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Crescent shaping"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " keeps the shawl from standing out from the shoulders."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "Fingering weight yarn",
              "qty": "450 m"
            },
            {
              "name": "3.5 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Blocking pins and mat",
              "qty": "1 set"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "2 shells x 8 rows = 10 x 10 cm in shell stitch after blocking."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern notes"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Shell: 5 tr into the same ch-sp. Chain-1 between shells. Outer-edge increase: work 2 shells into the final chain space of each right-side row."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Foundation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chain 30. Row 1 (right side): dc in 4th ch from hook, * ch 1, skip 2, 5 tr in next ch (shell), ch 1, skip 2, dc; rep from * to end. Turn. (4 shells)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 2 (wrong side): ch 3, dc into each ch-1 sp with ch 1 between. Turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 3 (right side): ch 3, dc, * ch 1, "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "shell-stitch-l2"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "shell"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " in ch-sp, ch 1, dc; rep. At outer (right) edge work 2 shells into final ch-sp (increase). Turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Repeat rows 2 and 3, adding one extra shell at the outer edge of every right-side row. Work to 22 cm depth (about 18 rows) or until yarn is almost used."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Border"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work 1 round of dc evenly along all edges, placing 3 dc at each point. Fasten off."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in ends. Wet the shawl and pin to a full crescent shape on a blocking mat. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking-l2"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Blocking"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " sets the curve and opens the shells. Leave flat until dry."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to crochet next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The rectangular lace shawl uses a dc mesh on a straight rectangle. It is the simplest shape in the collection."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
